From 791519fabab6f7ee48c9625c13d7ebe97c76d0cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xin-osaka-u <329067957+xin-osaka-u@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:20:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] QSA: multi-group pending index-K ring so NEXTN verify windows
 wider than the compress ratio fit

The per-request pending ring held one compression group (slot = req*ratio + pos%ratio).
A speculative-paged forward scatters the whole verify window before compressing any
group, so a window not aligned to the ratio overwrote the open group's committed keys
(the "W4 prefix-tail alias": the closed group was averaged over the shifted window and
carried the wrong RoPE position) and windows wider than the ratio were rejected outright.

The ring now holds N = ceil((draft_tokens + ratio - 1) / ratio) groups per request
(2 for a 4-token window, 3 for 8); slot = req*ratio*N + pos % (ratio*N) in the host
builders and the CUDA-graph Triton kernel alike. The verify guard allows
draft_tokens <= ratio*N - (ratio-1). N is derived from the server's maximum draft
tokens at pool construction; SGLANG_QSA_RING_GROUPS overrides it (1 = legacy layout).
PD transfer items cover a whole request ring. Offline replay (tools/qsa_ring/ring_test_sim.py in the recipe repo)
shows the legacy layout aliasing 81% of the keys closed inside 4-token windows and the
new sizing aliasing none; the graph kernel matches the host builders for N=1,2,3,5.

Based on the idea of sgl-project/sglang#40143 with the corrected group count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
